    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2d1cdd39-5ce3-562a-b22b-4d08c8669037",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 7$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=7,$ and since $B$ is formed by $1$ vector, $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 1+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-1 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
